course: dictionary
lesson: 11832
title: Blah, blah, blah: informal words
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words are informal. You use them when chatting with friends, not when writing a school report or a letter. «Blah» is one of these words.
explain: When someone talks on and on about nothing interesting, you can say «blah blah blah». The words stand in for boring or empty talk. «Mum said, "Tidy your room, eat your greens, blah blah blah," so I stopped listening.»
explain: Blah can also mean feeling dull or fed up. Someone with «the blahs» feels a bit low and not very interested in anything. Remember that blah belongs in chat, never in formal writing.
fact: «Blah» is an informal word, so keep it for chatting, not for formal writing.
fact: «Blah blah blah» means boring or empty talk.
fact: «Blah» can stand in for the rest of something that is obvious or boring: «We need milk, eggs, bread, blah.»
fact: «The blahs» means feeling dull and fed up.
fact: In the US, «blah» can also be an adjective meaning dull or not interesting.
exercise: «Mum said, "Tidy up, eat your greens, blah blah blah," so I stopped listening.» What does blah blah blah mean here? | Very good news | A loud song | The name of a person | *Boring or empty talk
exercise: «The rules are simple: wear a helmet, ride on the path, blah.» What does blah stand for? | *The rest of the rules, which are obvious or boring | A famous race | A type of bike | A sudden storm
exercise: Which sentence is a good place for blah? | *«Ugh, this homework is so blah.» said to a friend | «The poem uses blah imagery.» | «Dear Head Teacher, the school trip is blah.» | «The scientist recorded blah results.»
test: Jake says, «I've got the blahs today.» What does he probably feel? | Excited about a party | Top of the class | Very hot and sweaty | *Dull and fed up
test: Which word is informal, so it belongs in chat rather than formal writing? | *blah | ancient | curt | famished
exam: Ella writes in a school essay, «The author's ideas were blah.» Is this a good choice? | Yes, blah is a formal word that means excellent | *No, blah is informal and does not belong in a formal essay | No, because blah only means a type of food | Yes, because blah means very excited
